apa, and the priest Vasistha, together with other excellent twice-born ones.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-12-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1011006","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5d5a30c5b644c403fef492138e1140383f66ee368ffe3a70447ce3130d19afd3","compact":"7bdc27ec199d326d43f15d4362d8e9d30de6737836f882a6c2a86419dd234e5d","nasal":"fbe15c59a8fcfc4c9c4d5eea0cb527923b09cc6c75d253c80a4e32947948150b"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-11-7","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":11,"verse":7,"english":"They were Suyajña, and Vămadeva, and Jabali, and Kasyapa, and Vasistha, and other principal twice-born ones. And having paid homage to them, the virtuous king Dasaratha then spoke to them these sweet words.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-8-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1011007","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cdc7c0273328bc0966bed169fc6c93f2774ff19f9d8e63ecbab08d70f5fbb1c1","compact":"7bf59051b4a5796f6b9aad617292a946d06db94189e9d8951fbc04a88dafc22a","nasal":"7bf59051b4a5796f6b9aad617292a946d06db94189e9d8951fbc04a88dafc22a"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-11-8","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":11,"verse":8,"english":"Aggrieved on account of a son, I have no happiness on earth, and, therefore, I have intended to celebrate a horse-sacrifice.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.82,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-12-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1011008","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a9f3bac2d7e1428de0b840d10214591ec239bcdbae6e1ee1f92d34775a0ced51","compact":"38d221f893560ad1ece6ad1855bf302cffa60af75241904ad848975a10209948","nasal":"38d221f893560ad1ece6ad1855bf302cffa60af75241904ad848975a10209948"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-11-9","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":11,"verse":9,"english":"So, I would like to perform a horse-sacrifice. And by the grace of the saint's son, I shall obtain my desire.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.625,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-12-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1011009","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3ae142137840f1d8b2de632ed8cb4a2df4d5e7e00018d40a181317ad72f267ff","compact":"7b5fb9a0c10f82504ce76161d055e1e9760391eb5d5b3ebad2f26c7cd389a229","nasal":"7b5fb9a0c10f82504ce76161d055e1e9760391eb5d5b3ebad2f26c7cd389a229"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-11-10","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":11,"verse":10,"english":"Thereupon, the Brāhmaṇas with Vasiştha at their head honoured the words that fell from the king's lips, saying, Well!","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-12-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1011010","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1cf56e0a6dc972266a6dcc04086b692457f0bbc4eb1eb5c55ade99be24568cf2","compact":"a712199749cf87272b1217d295bfb28b3876936723b5248a71d18e2e005370cc","nasal":"a712199749cf87272b1217d295bfb28b3876936723b5248a71d18e2e005370cc"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-11-11","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":11,"verse":11,"english":"The Brāhmaṇas headed by Rsyaśộnga addressed the king, saying, Do you arrange for the provisions, loose the horse, and prepare the sacrificial ground on the north bank of the Sarayū river!","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.757,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-12-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1011011","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"289b57cfa1dbb35b112d9dac2ab07801917e5b10b3e4f33ef0ef06c358cf060b","compact":"